Short:        680x0 learning utility with applications board
Uploader:     a duffy staffs ac uk (Andrew Duffy)
Type:         dev/asm
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Authors:      a.duffy@staffs.ac.uk (Andrew Duffy), c.morris@staffs.ac.uk (Chris Morris)

AmigaFlight is a freely distributable 68000 learning utility that provides many
pre-programmed subroutines to eliminate the need for learning the internal
workings of the Amiga Operating System.

AmigaFlight is for AmigaOS 2.0+ machines only.

Below is a run-down of the most important features of AmigaFlight:

    o Simple to use environment
    o Applications board consists of many control and output windows
    o Works with all CPU's, including 68040
    o Uses Workbench 2 `newlook' screen (clones Workbench mode)
    o Uses AppIcons and AppMenuItems
    o Conditional WB3 code to take advantage of new functions
    o Comes with documentation in AmigaGuide format
    o Substantial on-line AmigaGuide Help system
    o Installation scripts for Installer
    o Fully configurable environment
